[00:15.16]1. Who is your friend, O God?
[00:20.04]Who in your tent may dwell?
[00:24.92]Who gains your friendship? Who gains your trust?
[00:29.80]Who really knows you well?
[00:32.28]All who embrace your Word,
[00:34.75]All who have faith in you,
[00:44.44]All who are loyal, all who are just,
[00:48.94]Living the truth for you.
[01:09.69]2. Who is your friend, O God?
[01:13.69]Who may approach your throne?
[01:17.69]Who brings delight and makes you rejoice?
[01:23.69]Whose name to you is known?
[01:28.41]All who exalt your name,
[01:32.61]All who your Word obey,
[01:37.61]All who are faithful, honest in heart,
[01:43.96]Truthful in all they say.
[01:50.30]3. Throwing our cares on you,
[01:59.98]Baring our hearts in prayer,
[02:03.26]Drawing us closer, bonding in love,
[02:06.54]Feeling your daily care,
[02:10.75]We yearn to be your friend.
[02:14.51]Long may our friendship grow.
[02:19.23]No greater Friend could we ever gain,
[02:24.23]No greater Friend we’ll know.